			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Former WWE and TNA star signed legends contract with WWE</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/wwe-news/397695-former-wwe-and-tna-star-signed-legends-contract-with-wwe/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/wwe-news/397695-former-wwe-and-tna-star-signed-legends-contract-with-wwe/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:04:37 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[WWE News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Ken Anderson]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Legends deal]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397695</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Former WWE and TNA star Ken Anderson announced on Saturday during Big Event EXS at the Suffolk Credit&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/wwe-news/397695-former-wwe-and-tna-star-signed-legends-contract-with-wwe/">Former WWE and TNA star signed legends contract with WWE</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Former WWE and TNA star Ken Anderson announced on Saturday during Big Event EXS at the Suffolk Credit Union Arena, in Brentwood, New York, he has signed a legends contract with WWE.</p>



<iframe loading="lazy" src="https://www.facebook.com/plugins/video.php?href=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2Freel%2F962010926703160%2F&#038;show_text=0&#038;width=267" width="267" height="476" style="border:none;overflow:hidden" scrolling="no" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen="true" allow="autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; picture-in-picture; web-share" allowFullScreen="true"></iframe>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Anderson wrestled in WWE as Ken Kennedy and Mr. Kennedy from 2005 to 2009. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Anderson was released from his WWE contract on May 29, 2009. He said his release was due to Randy Orton complaining to WWE management that he (Anderson), was reckless in the ring, saying  a botched backdrop caused him (Orton) to land on his head and neck instead of his back. Orton said the move could have possibility ended his career. Anderson also said that Orton persuaded John Cena to complain to Vince McMahon about his (Anderson&#8217;s) in-ring performance, which then prompted McMahon to release him from his contract.  In 2020, Anderson and Orton resolved their issues over the botched incident.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Anderson then went on to sign with TNA Wrestling in 2010 and spent six-years with the company. He was released in March for failing a drug test. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He returned to TNA on the September 18 episode of IMPACT, aligning himself with  Steve Maclin in his feud with Frankie Kazarian for the International Championship.</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/wwe-news/397695-former-wwe-and-tna-star-signed-legends-contract-with-wwe/">Former WWE and TNA star signed legends contract with WWE</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/wwe-news/397695-former-wwe-and-tna-star-signed-legends-contract-with-wwe/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
	</channel>
</rss>
